      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIELD OF FLUTES (1) sets the standard after stringing together three wins, the latest in an Open over 1300m at this track after he had already taken out a BM76 here over 1200m. He returns to 1000m with a strong track-and-distance record and Jarrod Todd has an excellent association with him, so the big weight looks the main task rather than a reason to oppose him. WALLENDA (6) resumes after five months and has enough merit in his previous campaign to be a genuine danger, with the interrupted BM76 eighth before the break better than it reads and his 1000m record a positive. FORMS OF FEAR (4) also resumes and his two runs before spelling were plain, but he has won at this track and distance and Raymond Vigar back aboard strengthens the place case. FLYING ANNIE (7) has been honest in BM76 company, placing last start and finishing close up the run prior, though she still has to turn consistency into a sharper winning blow.",
